[2026-03-16T04:00:39.129Z] {"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_012EgArio36x6UJe3BroVC9k","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→# AirbnbClone Test Specification\n     2→\n     3→## Page: Login / Register (`/login`)\n     4→\n     5→<!-- Components: LoginForm, RegisterForm, AuthToggle -->\n     6→\n     7→### Component: AuthToggle\n     8→\n     9→#### Test: Auth page defaults to login mode\n    10→- **Initial state:** User navigates to `/login` for the first time (not logged in).\n    11→- **Expected:** The page displays in login mode with the email input field visible, a \"Log In\" submit button, and a toggle link reading \"Don't have an account? Register\" at the bottom.\n    12→\n    13→#### Test: Toggle from login to register mode\n    14→- **Initial state:** User is on `/login` in login mode.\n    15→- **Action:** User clicks the \"Don't have an account? Register\" link.\n    16→- **Expected:** The form switches to register mode showing name and email fields, a \"Register\" submit button, and the toggle link changes to \"Already have an account? Log In\".\n    17→\n    18→#### Test: Toggle from register back to login mode\n    19→- **Initial state:** User is on `/login` in register mode.\n    20→- **Action:** User clicks the \"Already have an account? Log In\" link.\n    21→- **Expected:** The form switches back to login mode with only the email field and \"Log In\" button visible.\n    22→\n    23→#### Test: Toggle preserves no stale input between modes\n    24→- **Initial state:** User is on `/login` in login mode.\n    25→- **Action:** User types \"test@example.com\" in the email field, then toggles to register mode.\n    26→- **Expected:** The register form fields are empty (no carried-over email value).\n    27→\n    28→### Component: LoginForm\n    29→\n    30→#### Test: Login with valid email redirects to home\n    31→- **Initial state:** User is on `/login` in login mode. A user with email \"guest@example.com\" exists in the database.\n    32→- **Action:** User types \"guest@example.com\" in the email input and clicks the \"Log In\" button.\n    33→- **Expected:** The app calls `POST /api/auth` with the email, stores the returned user object in Redux state, and redirects to the home page (`/`).\n    34→\n    35→#### Test: Login with empty email shows validation error\n    36→- **Initial state:** User is on `/login` in login mode.\n    37→- **Action:** User clicks the \"Log In\" button without entering an email.\n    38→- **Expected:** A validation error message is displayed (e.g., \"Email is required\"). No API call is made.\n    39→\n    40→#### Test: Login with invalid email format shows validation error\n    41→- **Initial state:** User is on `/login` in login mode.\n    42→- **Action:** User types \"not-an-email\" in the email field and clicks \"Log In\".\n    43→- **Expected:** A validation error message is displayed (e.g., \"Please enter a valid email address\"). No API call is made.\n    44→\n    45→#### Test: Login with non-existent email shows error\n    46→- **Initial state:** User is on `/login` in login mode. No user with email \"unknown@example.com\" exists.\n    47→- **Action:** User types \"unknown@example.com\" and clicks \"Log In\".\n    48→- **Expected:** An error message is displayed (e.g., \"No account found with this email\"). The user remains on the login page.\n    49→\n    50→#### Test: Login form email input is functional on repeated use\n    51→- **Initial state:** User is on `/login` in login mode.\n    52→- **Action:** User types \"wrong@example.com\", submits and gets an error, then clears the field, types \"guest@example.com\", and clicks \"Log In\" again.\n    53→- **Expected:** The second submission succeeds, the user is logged in and redirected to home.\n    54→\n    55→### Component: RegisterForm\n    56→\n    57→#### Test: Register with valid name and email creates account and redirects to home\n    58→- **Initial state:** User is on `/login` in register mode. No user with email \"newuser@example.com\" exists.\n    59→- **Action:** User types \"New User\" in the name field and \"newuser@example.com\" in the email field, then clicks \"Register\".\n    60→- **Expected:** The app calls `POST /api/auth` with name and email, stores the returned user object in Redux state, and redirects to the home page (`/`).\n    61→\n    62→#### Test: Register with empty name shows validation error\n    63→- **Initial state:** User is on `/login` in register mode.\n    64→- **Action:** User types \"newuser@example.com\" in the email field but leaves the name field empty, then clicks \"Register\".\n    65→- **Expected:** A validation error is displayed (e.g., \"Name is required\"). No API call is made.\n    66→\n    67→#### Test: Register with empty email shows validation error\n    68→- **Initial state:** User is on `/login` in register mode.\n    69→- **Action:** User types \"New User\" in the name field but leaves the email field empty, then clicks \"Register\".\n    70→- **Expected:** A validation error is displayed (e.g., \"Email is required\"). No API call is made.\n    71→\n    72→#### Test: Register with invalid email format shows validation error\n    73→- **Initial state:** User is on `/login` in register mode.\n    74→- **Action:** User types \"New User\" in the name field and \"bad-email\" in the email field, then clicks \"Register\".\n    75→- **Expected:** A validation error is displayed (e.g., \"Please enter a valid email address\"). No API call is made.\n    76→\n    77→#### Test: Register with already-existing email shows error\n    78→- **Initial state:** User is on `/login` in register mode. A user with email \"existing@example.com\" already exists.\n    79→- **Action:** User types \"Some Name\" in the name field and \"existing@example.com\" in the email field, then clicks \"Register\".\n    80→- **Expected:** An error message is displayed (e.g., \"An account with this email already exists\"). The user remains on the register form.\n    81→\n    82→#### Test: Register form fields are functional on repeated use\n    83→- **Initial state:** User is on `/login` in register mode.\n    84→- **Action:** User fills in name and an already-existing email, submits and gets an error, then changes the email to a new unique email and clicks \"Register\" again.\n    85→- **Expected:** The second submission succeeds, the user is registered and redirected to home.\n    86→\n    87→### Component: E2E Auth Flow\n    88→\n    89→#### Test: Complete signup, signout, and signin flow\n    90→- **Initial state:** User navigates to `/login` (not logged in). No account exists for the test email.\n    91→- **Action:** User toggles to register mode, fills in a unique name and email, and clicks \"Register\". After being redirected to the home page, the user opens the sidebar menu and clicks \"Log out\". The user then navigates to `/login`, enters the same email used during registration, and clicks \"Log In\".\n    92→- **Expected:** After registration, the user is redirected to the home page (`/`). After logging out, a \"Log in\" link is visible in the header. After logging in with the previously registered email, the user is redirected back to the home page (`/`), confirming the account was persisted and the full auth round-trip works.\n    93→\n    94→## Page: Home / Search (`/`)\n    95→\n    96→<!-- Components: SearchBar, CategoryFilter, PropertyGrid, PropertyCard, FavoriteButton, FiltersPanel, Pagination -->\n    97→\n    98→### Component: SearchBar\n    99→\n   100→#### Test: Search bar displays all input fields on load\n   101→- **Initial state:** User navigates to the home page (`/`).\n   102→- **Expected:** The search bar is visible at the top of the page containing four inputs: a location text input with placeholder \"Where are you going?\", a check-in date picker, a check-out date picker, and a guest count selector. A search/submit button with a magnifying glass icon is visible.\n   103→\n   104→#### Test: Search by location filters property results\n   105→- **Initial state:** User is on the home page. Properties exist in \"Paris\", \"New York\", and \"Tokyo\".\n   106→- **Action:** User types \"Paris\" into the location input and clicks the search button.\n   107→- **Expected:** The property grid updates to show only properties where the city matches \"Paris\". Properties in other cities are not displayed.\n   108→\n   109→#### Test: Search by check-in and check-out dates filters results\n   110→- **Initial state:** User is on the home page. Some properties have bookings that overlap with the selected dates.\n   111→- **Action:** User selects a check-in date of \"2026-04-01\" and a check-out date of \"2026-04-05\" using the date pickers, then clicks the search button.\n   112→- **Expected:** The property grid updates to show only properties that are available (not fully booked) for the selected date range. The date pickers display the selected dates in a readable format.\n   113→\n   114→#### Test: Search by guest count filters results\n   115→- **Initial state:** User is on the home page. Properties exist with max_guests values of 2, 4, and 8.\n   116→- **Action:** User sets the guest count to 5 and clicks the search button.\n   117→- **Expected:** The property grid updates to show only properties where max_guests >= 5. Properties with fewer guest capacity are hidden.\n   118→\n   119→#### Test: Combined search with all fields filters results\n   120→- **Initial state:** User is on the home page. Multiple properties exist with varying locations, availability, and guest capacities.\n   121→- **Action:** User types \"New York\" in the location field, selects check-in \"2026-05-10\" and check-out \"2026-05-15\", sets guests to 3, and clicks the search button.\n   122→- **Expected:** The property grid shows only properties in New York that are available for those dates and accommodate at least 3 guests.\n   123→\n   124→#### Test: Clearing search fields and re-searching shows all results\n   125→- **Initial state:** User has performed a search for \"Paris\" and the grid shows filtered results.\n   126→- **Action:** User clears the location field (making it empty) and clicks the search button.\n   127→- **Expected:** The property grid resets to show all properties (unfiltered by location).\n   128→\n   129→#### Test: Search bar is functional on repeated use\n   130→- **Initial state:** User is on the home page.\n   131→- **Action:** User searches for \"Paris\", views results, then clears the location field, types \"Tokyo\", and searches again.\n   132→- **Expected:** The first search shows only Paris properties. After the second search, the grid updates to show only Tokyo properties. The location input correctly reflects \"Tokyo\".\n   133→\n   134→#### Test: Check-in date picker prevents selecting past dates\n   135→- **Initial state:** User is on the home page.\n   136→- **Action:** User opens the check-in date picker.\n   137→- **Expected:** Dates before today are disabled/grayed out and cannot be selected.\n   138→\n   139→#### Test: Check-out date must be after check-in date\n   140→- **Initial state:** User is on the home page and has selected a check-in date of \"2026-04-10\".\n   141→- **Action:** User opens the check-out date picker.\n   142→- **Expected:** Dates on or before \"2026-04-10\" are disabled/grayed out and cannot be selected. Only dates after the check-in date are selectable.\n   143→\n   144→#### Test: Guest count selector enforces minimum of 1\n   145→- **Initial state:** User is on the home page.\n   146→- **Action:** User interacts with the guest count selector.\n   147→- **Expected:** The minimum selectable value is 1. The user cannot set the guest count to 0 or a negative number.\n   148→\n   149→### Component: CategoryFilter\n   150→\n   151→#### Test: Category filter bar displays all property type chips\n   152→- **Initial state:** User navigates to the home page (`/`).\n   153→- **Expected:** A horizontal scrollable bar of category chips is displayed below the search bar. Chips are shown for each property type: \"Apartment\", \"House\", \"Cabin\", \"Villa\", \"Condo\", \"Loft\", \"Cottage\", \"Townhouse\". No chip is selected by default (all properties are shown).\n   154→\n   155→#### Test: Clicking a category chip filters properties by that type\n   156→- **Initial state:** User is on the home page. Properties of various types exist (apartments, houses, cabins, etc.).\n   157→- **Action:** User clicks the \"Cabin\" chip.\n   158→- **Expected:** The \"Cabin\" chip becomes visually selected/highlighted (e.g., bold outline or filled background). The property grid updates to show only properties with property_type \"Cabin\".\n   159→\n   160→#### Test: Clicking the selected category chip deselects it and shows all properties\n   161→- **Initial state:** User is on the home page with the \"Cabin\" chip currently selected.\n   162→- **Action:** User clicks the \"Cabin\" chip again.\n   163→- **Expected:** The \"Cabin\" chip returns to its unselected appearance. The property grid shows all properties again (no category filter applied).\n   164→\n   165→#### Test: Switching between category chips updates the filter\n   166→- **Initial state:** User is on the home page with the \"Cabin\" chip selected, showing only cabin properties.\n   167→- **Action:** User clicks the \"Villa\" chip.\n   168→- **Expected:** The \"Cabin\" chip becomes unselected and the \"Villa\" chip becomes selected/highlighted. The property grid updates to show only properties with property_type \"Villa\".\n   169→\n   170→#### Test: Category filter works in combination with search bar\n   171→- **Initial state:** User is on the home page. Properties exist: a cabin in Paris, an apartment in Paris, and a cabin in Tokyo.\n   172→- **Action:** User types \"Paris\" in the search bar location field and clicks search, then clicks the \"Cabin\" chip.\n   173→- **Expected:** The property grid shows only cabin properties in Paris. Both the search and category filters are applied simultaneously.\n   174→\n   175→#### Test: Category filter bar is horizontally scrollable when chips overflow\n   176→- **Initial state:** User is on the home page on a narrow viewport where all chips don't fit in one row.\n   177→- **Expected:** The category filter bar is horizontally scrollable. The user can scroll left/right to see all property type chips.\n   178→\n   179→#### Test: Category chip is functional on repeated use\n   180→- **Initial state:** User is on the home page.\n   181→- **Action:** User clicks \"Apartment\" (filtered), then clicks \"House\" (switches filter), then clicks \"House\" again (deselects), then clicks \"Cabin\" (filtered again).\n   182→- **Expected:** Each click correctly updates the selected chip and the property grid filters. The final state shows only cabin properties with the \"Cabin\" chip highlighted.\n   183→\n   184→### Component: PropertyGrid\n   185→\n   186→#### Test: Property grid displays properties in a responsive grid layout\n   187→- **Initial state:** User navigates to the home page. Multiple properties exist in the database.\n   188→- **Expected:** Properties are displayed in a responsive grid: 1 column on mobile, 2 columns on tablet, 3-4 columns on desktop. Each property is rendered as a PropertyCard.\n   189→\n   190→#### Test: Property grid shows message when no properties match filters\n   191→- **Initial state:** User is on the home page.\n   192→- **Action:** User searches for a location with no matching properties (e.g., \"Atlantis\").\n   193→- **Expected:** The property grid area displays a \"No properties found\" message instead of an empty grid. The message suggests adjusting filters or search criteria.\n   194→\n   195→#### Test: Property grid loads and displays properties from API on initial page load\n   196→- **Initial state:** User navigates to the home page. Properties exist in the database.\n   197→- **Expected:** The grid fetches properties via `GET /api/properties` and displays property cards. While loading, a loading indicator is shown. Once loaded, the property cards appear with correct data.\n   198→\n   199→### Component: PropertyCard\n   200→\n   201→#### Test: Property card displays all required information\n   202→- **Initial state:** User is on the home page. A property exists with title \"Cozy Cabin\", city \"Aspen\", country \"US\", property_type \"Cabin\", price_per_night 150, an average rating of 4.5, and 12 reviews.\n   203→- **Expected:** The property card shows: the main property image at the top, a \"Cabin\" property type badge, the title \"Cozy Cabin\", location \"Aspen, US\", \"$150 / night\" price, and a star icon with \"4.5 (12 reviews)\" rating display.\n   204→\n   205→#### Test: Property card shows property image\n   206→- **Initial state:** User is on the home page. A property exists with at least one image (the first image by display_order).\n   207→- **Expected:** The property card displays the main image (lowest display_order) at the top of the card with rounded top corners. If no image exists, a placeholder image is shown.\n   208→\n   209→#### Test: Clicking a property card navigates to property detail page\n   210→- **Initial state:** User is on the home page. A property with id \"abc-123\" is displayed.\n   211→- **Action:** User clicks on the property card (not the favorite button).\n   212→- **Expected:** The app navigates to `/properties/abc-123` (the property detail page).\n   213→\n   214→#### Test: Property card displays property type badge\n   215→- **Initial state:** User is on the home page. Properties of different types exist.\n   216→- **Expected:** Each property card shows a badge/label indicating the property type (e.g., \"Apartment\", \"House\", \"Cabin\"). The badge is visually distinct (e.g., small colored label overlaying or near the image).\n   217→\n   218→#### Test: Property card displays average rating with review count\n   219→- **Initial state:** User is on the home page. A property has an average rating of 4.2 from 8 reviews.\n   220→- **Expected:** The card shows a star icon with \"4.2\" and \"(8 reviews)\" or \"(8)\" next to it. If the property has no reviews, the rating section shows \"New\" or is not displayed.\n   221→\n   222→### Component: FavoriteButton\n   223→\n   224→#### Test: Favorite button shows outline heart when property is not favorited\n   225→- **Initial state:** User is logged in and on the home page. The property is not in the user's favorites.\n   226→- **Expected:** The property card displays a heart icon with an outline (unfilled) style in the top-right corner of the card image.\n   227→\n   228→#### Test: Clicking favorite button on unfavorited property adds it to favorites\n   229→- **Initial state:** User is logged in and on the home page. A property is not in their favorites.\n   230→- **Action:** User clicks the heart icon on the property card.\n   231→- **Expected:** The app calls `POST /api/favorites` with the property ID. The heart icon changes to a filled/solid red heart. The property is now in the user's favorites list.\n   232→\n   233→#### Test: Clicking favorite button on favorited property removes it from favorites\n   234→- **Initial state:** User is logged in and on the home page. A property is already in their favorites (heart is filled/red).\n   235→- **Action:** User clicks the filled heart icon on the property card.\n   236→- **Expected:** The app calls `DELETE /api/favorites/:propertyId`. The heart icon changes back to an outline (unfilled) style. The property is removed from the user's favorites.\n   237→\n   238→#### Test: Favorite button does not navigate to property detail page\n   239→- **Initial state:** User is logged in and on the home page.\n   240→- **Action:** User clicks the heart icon on a property card.\n   241→- **Expected:** The favorite is toggled but the user remains on the home page. The click does not propagate to the card's navigation handler.\n   242→\n   243→#### Test: Favorite button is not shown when user is not logged in\n   244→- **Initial state:** User is not logged in and is on the home page.\n   245→- **Expected:** Property cards do not display the heart/favorite icon. Alternatively, clicking the heart redirects the user to the login page.\n   246→\n   247→#### Test: Favorite button reflects correct state on page load\n   248→- **Initial state:** User is logged in and has previously favorited two properties. User navigates to the home page.\n   249→- **Expected:** The app calls `GET /api/favorites` to fetch the user's favorites. The two favorited properties show filled/red hearts. All other properties show outline hearts.\n   250→\n   251→#### Test: Favorite button is functional on repeated use\n   252→- **Initial state:** User is logged in and on the home page with a property that is not favorited.\n   253→- **Action:** User clicks the heart icon (favorites it), then clicks it again (unfavorites it), then clicks it a third time (favorites it again).\n   254→- **Expected:** Each click correctly toggles the heart appearance and makes the appropriate API call. The final state is favorited (filled heart).\n   255→\n   256→### Component: FiltersPanel\n   257→\n   258→#### Test: Filters panel is hidden by default with a visible toggle button\n   259→- **Initial state:** User navigates to the home page (`/`).\n   260→- **Expected:** The filters panel is collapsed/hidden. A \"Filters\" button (with a filter icon) is visible that the user can click to open the panel.\n   261→\n   262→#### Test: Clicking the Filters button opens the filters panel\n   263→- **Initial state:** User is on the home page with the filters panel hidden.\n   264→- **Action:** User clicks the \"Filters\" button.\n   265→- **Expected:** The filters panel opens/expands, revealing all filter controls: a price range slider, bedrooms minimum selector, beds minimum selector, bathrooms minimum selector, and amenity checkboxes grouped by category.\n   266→\n   267→#### Test: Clicking the Filters button again closes the filters panel\n   268→- **Initial state:** User is on the home page with the filters panel open.\n   269→- **Action:** User clicks the \"Filters\" button again.\n   270→- **Expected:** The filters panel collapses/hides. The property grid remains showing the previously applied filters.\n   271→\n   272→#### Test: Price range slider filters properties by price per night\n   273→- **Initial state:** User is on the home page with the filters panel open. Properties exist with prices $50, $100, $200, and $500 per night.\n   274→- **Action:** User adjusts the price range slider to a minimum of $75 and a maximum of $250.\n   275→- **Expected:** The property grid updates to show only properties with price_per_night between $75 and $250 (i.e., $100 and $200 properties). The slider visually reflects the selected range with labels showing the min and max values.\n   276→\n   277→#### Test: Bedrooms minimum filter works correctly\n   278→- **Initial state:** User is on the home page with the filters panel open. Properties exist with 1, 2, 3, and 5 bedrooms.\n   279→- **Action:** User sets the bedrooms minimum selector to 3.\n   280→- **Expected:** The property grid updates to show only properties with 3 or more bedrooms.\n   281→\n   282→#### Test: Beds minimum filter works correctly\n   283→- **Initial state:** User is on the home page with the filters panel open. Properties exist with varying bed counts.\n   284→- **Action:** User sets the beds minimum selector to 2.\n   285→- **Expected:** The property grid updates to show only properties with 2 or more beds.\n   286→\n   287→#### Test: Bathrooms minimum filter works correctly\n   288→- **Initial state:** User is on the home page with the filters panel open. Properties exist with 1, 2, and 3 bathrooms.\n   289→- **Action:** User sets the bathrooms minimum selector to 2.\n   290→- **Expected:** The property grid updates to show only properties with 2 or more bathrooms.\n   291→\n   292→#### Test: Amenity checkboxes filter properties by selected amenities\n   293→- **Initial state:** User is on the home page with the filters panel open. Amenities include \"WiFi\", \"Pool\", \"Kitchen\", \"Parking\". Properties have varying amenities.\n   294→- **Action:** User checks the \"WiFi\" and \"Pool\" amenity checkboxes.\n   295→- **Expected:** The property grid updates to show only properties that have both WiFi AND Pool amenities. The checked amenities remain visually checked.\n   296→\n   297→#### Test: Amenity checkboxes are grouped by category\n   298→- **Initial state:** User is on the home page with the filters panel open.\n   299→- **Expected:** Amenity checkboxes are organized into groups labeled by category: \"Essentials\", \"Features\", \"Safety\", \"Location\". Each group contains the relevant amenities.\n   300→\n   301→#### Test: Multiple filters combine with AND logic\n   302→- **Initial state:** User is on the home page with the filters panel open.\n   303→- **Action:** User sets price range to $100–$300, bedrooms minimum to 2, and checks the \"WiFi\" amenity.\n   304→- **Expected:** The property grid shows only properties that satisfy ALL three conditions: price between $100–$300, at least 2 bedrooms, and has WiFi amenity.\n   305→\n   306→#### Test: Filters combine with search bar and category filter\n   307→- **Initial state:** User is on the home page. User has typed \"Paris\" in the search bar, selected \"Apartment\" category chip, and the filters panel is open.\n   308→- **Action:** User sets bedrooms minimum to 2 in the filters panel.\n   309→- **Expected:** The property grid shows only apartments in Paris with at least 2 bedrooms. All three filter mechanisms (search, category, filters panel) work together.\n   310→\n   311→#### Test: Resetting filters shows all properties\n   312→- **Initial state:** User is on the home page with multiple filters applied (price range, bedrooms, amenities).\n   313→- **Action:** User resets or clears all filter values back to their defaults (e.g., via a \"Clear Filters\" or \"Reset\" button, or manually resetting each).\n   314→- **Expected:** The property grid returns to showing all properties (unfiltered). All filter controls return to their default states.\n   315→\n   316→#### Test: Filters panel controls are functional on repeated use\n   317→- **Initial state:** User is on the home page with the filters panel open.\n   318→- **Action:** User sets bedrooms to 3 (filtered), then changes bedrooms back to 1, then sets bathrooms to 2, then unchecks and re-checks a \"WiFi\" amenity.\n   319→- **Expected:** Each change updates the property grid correctly. The final state reflects the last set of filter values (bedrooms >= 1, bathrooms >= 2, WiFi checked).\n   320→\n   321→### Component: Pagination\n   322→\n   323→#### Test: Pagination controls are displayed when results exceed one page\n   324→- **Initial state:** User is on the home page. More properties exist than can fit on one page (e.g., more than the page limit of 12 or 20 properties).\n   325→- **Expected:** Pagination controls are displayed below the property grid showing page numbers (e.g., \"1 2 3 ... 5\"), a \"Previous\" button (disabled on first page), and a \"Next\" button.\n   326→\n   327→#### Test: Pagination controls are hidden when all results fit on one page\n   328→- **Initial state:** User is on the home page. Fewer properties exist than the page limit.\n   329→- **Expected:** No pagination controls are displayed below the property grid.\n   330→\n   331→#### Test: Clicking Next page loads the next set of properties\n   332→- **Initial state:** User is on the home page viewing page 1 of results. Multiple pages of properties exist.\n   333→- **Action:** User clicks the \"Next\" button.\n   334→- **Expected:** The property grid updates to show the second page of properties. The URL or API call includes `page=2`. The current page indicator highlights \"2\". The \"Previous\" button becomes enabled.\n   335→\n   336→#### Test: Clicking Previous page loads the previous set of properties\n   337→- **Initial state:** User is on page 2 of property results.\n   338→- **Action:** User clicks the \"Previous\" button.\n   339→- **Expected:** The property grid updates to show the first page of properties. The current page indicator highlights \"1\". The \"Previous\" button becomes disabled again.\n   340→\n   341→#### Test: Clicking a specific page number navigates to that page\n   342→- **Initial state:** User is on page 1 of results. At least 3 pages of properties exist.\n   343→- **Action:** User clicks page number \"3\".\n   344→- **Expected:** The property grid updates to show the third page of properties. The current page indicator highlights \"3\".\n   345→\n   346→#### Test: Next button is disabled on the last page\n   347→- **Initial state:** User is on the last page of property results.\n   348→- **Expected:** The \"Next\" button is disabled/grayed out and not clickable. The \"Previous\" button is enabled.\n   349→\n   350→#### Test: Previous button is disabled on the first page\n   351→- **Initial state:** User is on page 1 of property results.\n   352→- **Expected:** The \"Previous\" button is disabled/grayed out and not clickable. The \"Next\" button is enabled (if more than one page exists).\n   353→\n   354→#### Test: Applying filters resets pagination to page 1\n   355→- **Initial state:** User is on page 3 of property results.\n   356→- **Action:** User applies a category filter by clicking the \"Cabin\" chip.\n   357→- **Expected:** The pagination resets to page 1. The property grid shows the first page of filtered results. The page indicator highlights \"1\".\n   358→\n   359→#### Test: Pagination is functional on repeated use\n   360→- **Initial state:** User is on page 1 of results with multiple pages available.\n   361→- **Action:** User clicks \"Next\" (goes to page 2), then clicks \"Next\" again (page 3), then clicks \"Previous\" (back to page 2), then clicks page \"1\" (back to page 1).\n   362→- **Expected:** Each navigation correctly updates the property grid and page indicator. The final state shows page 1 results.\n   363→\n   364→## Page: Property Detail (`/properties/:id`)\n   365→\n   366→<!-- Components: ImageGallery, PropertyHeader, PropertyInfo, PropertyDescription, AmenitiesList, BookingCard, ReviewsSection, HostInfoCard -->\n   367→\n   368→### Component: ImageGallery\n   369→\n   370→#### Test: Image gallery displays main large image and smaller thumbnails\n   371→- **Initial state:** User navigates to `/properties/:id` for a property with 5 images.\n   372→- **Expected:** The image gallery shows a grid layout with the first image (lowest display_order) displayed as a large main image, and the remaining images displayed as smaller thumbnails alongside or below it. All images have rounded corners.\n   373→\n   374→#### Test: Image gallery displays single image when property has only one image\n   375→- **Initial state:** User navigates to a property detail page for a property with exactly 1 image.\n   376→- **Expected:** The single image is displayed as the main large image. No thumbnail grid is shown.\n   377→\n   378→#### Test: Image gallery displays placeholder when property has no images\n   379→- **Initial state:** User navigates to a property detail page for a property with no images.\n   380→- **Expected:** A placeholder image or \"No images available\" message is displayed in the gallery area.\n   381→\n   382→#### Test: Clicking a thumbnail image makes it the main displayed image\n   383→- **Initial state:** User is on a property detail page with 5 images. The first image is displayed as the main image.\n   384→- **Action:** User clicks on the third thumbnail image.\n   385→- **Expected:** The third image becomes the main large image. The previously main image moves to the thumbnail grid.\n   386→\n   387→#### Test: Clicking thumbnails is functional on repeated use\n   388→- **Initial state:** User is on a property detail page with multiple images.\n   389→- **Action:** User clicks the second thumbnail, then the fourth thumbnail, then the first thumbnail.\n   390→- **Expected:** Each click updates the main image to the clicked thumbnail. The final state shows the first thumbnail as the main image.\n   391→\n   392→#### Test: Image gallery shows image captions when available\n   393→- **Initial state:** User navigates to a property detail page. The property has images with caption text set.\n   394→- **Expected:** Captions are displayed below or overlaying their respective images.\n   395→\n   396→### Component: PropertyHeader\n   397→\n   398→#### Test: Property header displays title, location, rating summary, and host info\n   399→- **Initial state:** User navigates to `/properties/:id` for a property with title \"Luxury Villa in Bali\", city \"Ubud\", country \"Indonesia\", an average rating of 4.7 from 23 reviews, hosted by \"Jane Host\" with an avatar.\n   400→- **Expected:** The property header shows the title \"Luxury Villa in Bali\", location \"Ubud, Indonesia\", a star icon with \"4.7\" and \"(23 reviews)\", and the host name \"Jane Host\" with their avatar image.\n   401→\n   402→#### Test: Property header shows \"New\" when property has no reviews\n   403→- **Initial state:** User navigates to a property detail page for a property with no reviews.\n   404→- **Expected:** The rating summary area shows \"New\" or no rating display instead of a numeric rating and review count.\n   405→\n   406→#### Test: Clicking review count scrolls to or navigates to reviews section\n   407→- **Initial state:** User is on a property detail page with reviews.\n   408→- **Action:** User clicks the \"(23 reviews)\" link in the property header.\n   409→- **Expected:** The page scrolls down to the ReviewsSection on the same page.\n   410→\n   411→#### Test: Property header displays host avatar as clickable element\n   412→- **Initial state:** User is on a property detail page. The host has an avatar_url set.\n   413→- **Expected:** The host's avatar image is displayed as a small circular image next to the host name. The host name is displayed next to the avatar.\n   414→\n   415→### Component: PropertyInfo\n   416→\n   417→#### Test: Property info section displays all property details\n   418→- **Initial state:** User navigates to `/properties/:id` for a property with property_type \"Villa\", max_guests 6, bedrooms 3, beds 4, bathrooms 2.\n   419→- **Expected:** The property info section displays: \"Villa\" as the property type, \"6 guests\", \"3 bedrooms\", \"4 beds\", and \"2 bathrooms\". Each detail has an appropriate icon.\n   420→\n   421→#### Test: Property info section displays check-in and check-out times\n   422→- **Initial state:** User navigates to a property detail page for a property with check_in_time \"15:00\" and check_out_time \"11:00\".\n   423→- **Expected:** The property info section shows check-in time as \"3:00 PM\" (or \"15:00\") and check-out time as \"11:00 AM\" (or \"11:00\").\n   424→\n   425→#### Test: Property info section handles singular and plural labels correctly\n   426→- **Initial state:** User navigates to a property detail page for a property with max_guests 1, bedrooms 1, beds 1, bathrooms 1.\n   427→- **Expected:** Labels display in singular form: \"1 guest\", \"1 bedroom\", \"1 bed\", \"1 bathroom\" (not \"1 guests\", etc.).\n   428→\n   429→### Component: PropertyDescription\n   430→\n   431→#### Test: Property description displays full description text\n   432→- **Initial state:** User navigates to `/properties/:id` for a property with a multi-paragraph description.\n   433→- **Expected:** The full property description text is displayed in a readable format with proper paragraph breaks.\n   434→\n   435→#### Test: Long description shows a \"Show more\" toggle\n   436→- **Initial state:** User navigates to a property detail page for a property with a very long description (multiple paragraphs).\n   437→- **Expected:** The description is initially truncated after a reasonable length with a \"Show more\" link/button visible at the bottom.\n   438→\n   439→#### Test: Clicking \"Show more\" expands the full description\n   440→- **Initial state:** User is on a property detail page with a truncated description and a visible \"Show more\" link.\n   441→- **Action:** User clicks the \"Show more\" link.\n   442→- **Expected:** The full description expands to show all text. The link changes to \"Show less\".\n   443→\n   444→#### Test: Clicking \"Show less\" collapses the description back\n   445→- **Initial state:** User is on a property detail page with the description fully expanded and a \"Show less\" link visible.\n   446→- **Action:** User clicks the \"Show less\" link.\n   447→- **Expected:** The description collapses back to the truncated view with \"Show more\" visible again.\n   448→\n   449→#### Test: Show more/less toggle is functional on repeated use\n   450→- **Initial state:** User is on a property detail page with a long description.\n   451→- **Action:** User clicks \"Show more\", then \"Show less\", then \"Show more\" again.\n   452→- **Expected:** Each click correctly toggles between the truncated and expanded states. The final state shows the full description.\n   453→\n   454→### Component: AmenitiesList\n   455→\n   456→#### Test: Amenities list displays amenities grouped by category with icons\n   457→- **Initial state:** User navigates to `/properties/:id` for a property with amenities including \"WiFi\" (Essentials), \"Pool\" (Features), \"Smoke Detector\" (Safety), \"Near Beach\" (Location).\n   458→- **Expected:** The amenities are displayed in groups with category headings: \"Essentials\", \"Features\", \"Safety\", \"Location\". Each amenity is shown with its icon and name.\n   459→\n   460→#### Test: Amenities list only shows categories that have amenities\n   461→- **Initial state:** User navigates to a property detail page. The property has amenities only in \"Essentials\" and \"Features\" categories (none in \"Safety\" or \"Location\").\n   462→- **Expected:** Only the \"Essentials\" and \"Features\" category groups are displayed. Empty categories are not shown.\n   463→\n   464→#### Test: Amenities list shows \"Show all amenities\" when there are many amenities\n   465→- **Initial state:** User navigates to a property detail page for a property with more than 10 amenities.\n   466→- **Expected:** An initial subset of amenities is displayed with a \"Show all X amenities\" button at the bottom (where X is the total count).\n   467→\n   468→#### Test: Clicking \"Show all amenities\" reveals the complete list\n   469→- **Initial state:** User is on a property detail page with many amenities and a \"Show all X amenities\" button visible.\n   470→- **Action:** User clicks \"Show all X amenities\".\n   471→- **Expected:** All amenities are displayed, grouped by category. The button changes to \"Show less\" or disappears.\n   472→\n   473→#### Test: Amenities list displays message when property has no amenities\n   474→- **Initial state:** User navigates to a property detail page for a property with no amenities.\n   475→- **Expected:** A message like \"No amenities listed\" is displayed, or the amenities section is not shown.\n   476→\n   477→### Component: BookingCard\n   478→\n   479→#### Test: Booking card displays price per night\n   480→- **Initial state:** User navigates to `/properties/:id` for a property with price_per_night $150.\n   481→- **Expected:** The booking card (sticky sidebar on desktop) shows \"$150 / night\" prominently at the top.\n   482→\n   483→#### Test: Booking card displays check-in and check-out date pickers\n   484→- **Initial state:** User is on a property detail page.\n   485→- **Expected:** The booking card contains a check-in date picker and a check-out date picker. Both are initially empty or show placeholder text.\n   486→\n   487→#### Test: Booking card displays guest count selector\n   488→- **Initial state:** User is on a property detail page for a property with max_guests 6.\n   489→- **Expected:** The booking card contains a guest count selector. The selector enforces a minimum of 1 and a maximum of 6 (the property's max_guests value).\n   490→\n   491→#### Test: Selecting dates and guests shows price breakdown\n   492→- **Initial state:** User is on a property detail page for a property with price_per_night $150 and cleaning_fee $75.\n   493→- **Action:** User selects check-in \"2026-05-01\" and check-out \"2026-05-04\" (3 nights) and sets guests to 2.\n   494→- **Expected:** The booking card displays a price breakdown: \"$150 x 3 nights = $450\", \"Cleaning fee: $75\", \"Total: $525\". The breakdown appears after both dates are selected.\n   495→\n   496→#### Test: Price breakdown updates when dates change\n   497→- **Initial state:** User is on a property detail page with check-in \"2026-05-01\" and check-out \"2026-05-04\" selected (3 nights).\n   498→- **Action:** User changes the check-out date to \"2026-05-06\" (5 nights).\n   499→- **Expected:** The price breakdown updates to reflect 5 nights: \"$150 x 5 nights = $750\", \"Cleaning fee: $75\", \"Total: $825\".\n   500→"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_015gnvCPVRMwFHcqNtBbjseH","session_id":"8726d00c-8026-4c68-978a-d437b7ce1755","uuid":"56660268-b3d0-4747-8bc4-c5c83a06b8f3"}
